* aif120_tuple_spec_regression.dts
* AIF-120 (application-ui-dsl) -- what the engine's tuple spec can say, measured, so
* the design table's BINDING can be judged against it instead of against VFP.
*
* R53 gave BINDING the syntax "alias.field" and refused everything else. BETA-4.4
* freezes the engine's own spec resolution as "*, AREA.*, AREA.FIELD, #n". This
* script measures all four against the shipped x64 school tables, so the gap between
* the two grammars is a run, not an argument. See AIF120_TUPLE_SPEC_V1.md.
*
* Form: transcript canary (the comment_handling_regression.dts form).
* Fixture: STUDENTS and ENROLL, read-only. One relation is added and cleared.
* Regression doctrine: every test sets its own environment.
*
* Run:  DOTSCRIPT aif120\aif120_tuple_spec_regression.dts
*
* EXPECTED OUTPUT -- the claims:
*   T1  bare field list          -> resolves          (this is NOT what R53 allows)
*   T2  *                        -> all fields of the current area
*   T3  AREA.FIELD               -> resolves, spanning two work areas  (R53's form)
*   T4  AREA.*                   -> all fields of a NAMED area
*   T5  #n ordinal               -> DOES NOT RESOLVE. The line degrades to a bare
*                                   TUPLE and prints every field, with no header,
*                                   because the canonical inline comment vocabulary
*                                   (AIF-037: && and #) cuts '#' to end of line
*                                   before the spec parser sees it. BETA-4.4 declares
*                                   a form the lexer removes.
*   T6  --AREA-PREFIX            -> headers qualify as AREA.FIELD
*   T7  --STRICT on a bad name   -> refuses, naming the area slot
*   G1  ERSATZ GRID          -> the body renders (PATH, DESCENDANT SUMMARY, TUPLE
*                                GRID, footer) while the header says
*                                "ROOT: (none)  RECNO: 0", CURRENT ROOT RECORD is
*                                "(none)" and RELATION TREE is "(none)".
*   G2  ERSATZ REFRESH        -> the SAME state renders as a complete five-region
*                                frame: ROOT/RECNO/PATH/LIMIT/ORDER, CURRENT ROOT
*                                RECORD, RELATION TREE, DESCENDANT SUMMARY, TUPLE
*                                GRID, and "ROWS SHOWN: n / LIMIT m | STATUS: OK".
*   G3  ERSATZ GRID again     -> STILL "ROOT: (none)". GRID is a second renderer
*                                ("ERSATZ GRID Relational Browser") that never
*                                resolves three of the five regions, and REFRESH
*                                ("ERSATZ Relational Browser") does. Same state.
*
*   The TUPLE GRID columns SPAN two work areas -- LNAME/FNAME/GENDER from STUDENTS,
*   CLS_ID/GRADE from ENROLL -- which is BETA-4.1's "one logical row; may span areas".

SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF
SET PATH DBF dbf/x64

FORMULA "AIF120-TUPLE-SPEC-BEGIN"

SELECT 1
USE STUDENTS
SELECT 2
USE ENROLL
SELECT 1
REL ADD STUDENTS ENROLL ON SID

ECHO T1 bare field list
TUPLE LNAME,FNAME --HEADER

ECHO T2 star
TUPLE * --HEADER

ECHO T3 AREA.FIELD across two areas
TUPLE STUDENTS.LNAME,ENROLL.GRADE --HEADER

ECHO T4 AREA.star
TUPLE ENROLL.* --HEADER

ECHO T5 ordinal -- expect NO header and every field
TUPLE #2,#3 --HEADER

ECHO T5b ordinal mid-spec -- expect LNAME alone, no header
TUPLE LNAME,#3 --HEADER

ECHO T6 area prefix
TUPLE STUDENTS.LNAME,ENROLL.GRADE --HEADER --AREA-PREFIX

ECHO T7 strict on a name that is not a field
TUPLE STUDENTS.NOSUCH --STRICT

ECHO
ECHO --- the grid the engine already ships ---
ERSATZ ROOT STUDENTS
ERSATZ LIMIT 3
ECHO G1 GRID -- header says ROOT (none), body is populated
ERSATZ GRID
ECHO G2 REFRESH -- the complete frame
ERSATZ REFRESH
ECHO G3 GRID again -- header is empty again
ERSATZ GRID

REL CLEAR ALL
WORKSPACE CLOSE

FORMULA "AIF120-TUPLE-SPEC-END"
